                    <physDesc>
                        <objectDesc>
                            <supportDesc>
                                <support><p>A fragment of a block of the local soft white limestone, with the surface finished and then red letters painted directly onto the stone. Intact on the right side, broken on the left and below, and perhaps incomplete at the top (the top appears to be worked and finished, perhaps to receive another block above). Modern plaster suppport added to the base. The rear is uneven and curves and is only roughly finished.</p>
                                    <material ana="#material.inorganic.stone.sedimentary_rock.limestone.calcarenite.whitish.iblei-orientali #material.inorganic.stone.sedimentary_rock.limestone.calcarenite.whitish.iblei-occidentali" type="stone.limestone.non-polishable.whitish" subtype="calcarenite_ibleiOR|calcarenite_ibleiOCC" resp="#Coccato" ref="http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/material/lod/30.html">whitish soft calcarenite with orangish patina, likely calcarenite degli Iblei (sand-grade limestone) (identification based on pXRF)</material>
                                    <objectType ana="#object.arch_element.wall" ref="http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/objtyp/lod/416.html">wall</objectType>
                                    <dimensions>
                                        <height unit="cm">23.5</height>
                                        <width unit="cm">15.3</width>
                                        <depth unit="cm">6.5</depth>
                                    </dimensions>
                                </support>
                                <condition ana="#condition.fragment"/>
		    </supportDesc>
                            <layoutDesc>
                                <layout><p>Traces of five lines of letters, vacat at the end of line 1.</p>
                                    <rs ana="#execution.painted" ref="http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/writing/lod/10">Painted</rs>
                                	<damage ana="#text_condition.incomplete"/>
			</layout>
                            </layoutDesc>
                        </objectDesc>
                        <handDesc>
                            <handNote><p>Finely painted Hellenistic letters in rigid style without serfis. Alpha has straight bar; epsilon has short middle bar; omicron is small and above the line (14-17 mm); omega is small, circular, closed, and almost sits on the line (19 mm).</p>
